# Coordinator ruling, phase 2 on dd4985e: the workaround that drops GTK 4.24.0's leaked GL context reference is a
# memory-safety risk of the 2.3.2 class. C: release -> resume churn across loops, part of it at load > 15. B: the fallback
# when the version gate (gate) or the reference-count check (refs, refused for real by an extra sink reference) does not match.
C1 churn: at least 100 release-resume cycles of a shed loop ran across the 8 loop files (@@ cycles, @@ resumes of a shed loop)
C3 churn: GL context and display threads never exceed one per loop file (peak @@ gstglcontext, @@ gldisplay-event, for 8 loop files; @@ and @@ once settled)
# C4 [ORIGINAL, superseded by C4-R1] still runs and prints as a SUPERSEDED line, not counted: its 3 s settle ended
# before the release and sweep bound, and dmabuf fds of the stills swing between samples (+17 right after the churn, +2 after one more pass, dd4985e o11m-run).
# C4-R1 [superseded by C4-R2, coordinator ruling on dd4985e] also prints as a SUPERSEDED line: the stills' dmabuf fds
# swing by up to +17 between settled samples without growing with the cycles. C4-R2 judges other fds and dmabuf apart.
C4-R2 churn: open files other than dmabuf do not grow beyond one per loop file 12 s after the last release (@@ since the first pass), and the stills' dmabuf fds do not grow between the churn halves (median @@ then @@, for 8 loop files)
C5 churn: loops still move when shown, during the churn and after it (@@ of @@ sampled)
